## Result

`make test` exited 0 unattended at 2026-11-01T22:40:47Z. Both installed clients
ran: Claude Code 2.1.304 and codex-cli 0.164.0. Five probe scripts exited 0;
13 candidate witnesses matched expectations (7 positive, including the tolerated
parent case, and 6 negative), with zero skips or timeouts. The stdout, stderr,
commands, CLI exits, model-input extracts, request hashes, and script exits are
committed in p0-resume-probe-evidence.log. Its line 8 records the actual gate
command and exit code; line 36 records the aggregate probe result.

A candidate's verdict is CLI exit 0 AND turn one in a captured model request.
`verdict_exit` is 0 for that result, otherwise 1. A negative record's PASS means
the candidate failed that predicate as required. Count-token requests and CLI
stdout cannot supply history evidence. Positive candidates also assert turn two.

