## Files and mechanisms

- Makefile:9 — canonical P0 gate runs source/witness checks and all probes;
  :11 exposes `make test-probes` independently.
- probes/support.py:42 — allowlisted environment and throwaway homes; :76 bounds
  child processes; :125 uses Claude `--bare` (installed help says no keychain
  reads); :136 creates fixtures with O_EXCL and mode 0600; :205 owns loopback
  streaming mocks; :286 computes the verdict from real model-input requests.
- probes/claude_resume.py:16 and probes/claude_api_records.py:10 — native id,
  external-path and snapshot-absence witnesses with malformed identity chains.
- probes/codex_rollout.py:16 and probes/codex_reasoning.py:10 — no-database
  fallback, read-only backfill observation, summary preservation, missing-meta
  negative controls.
- probes/codex_importer.py:21 — finite completion polling, not importId claims;
  :36 checks the installed schema; :57 separates staging HOME from CODEX_HOME;
  :98 reads Codex's own output and copies it to a fresh malformed candidate.
- probes/rpc.py:53 — bounded stdio RPC, initialize handshake and request ids;
  :72 checks app-server's actual shutdown exit.
- probes/resume.sh and probes/run.py — unattended entry point; independent
  scripts all run and their exit statuses determine the aggregate verdict.
- probes/check.py:22 — attribution, standard-library dependency inventory,
  shell syntax, fabricated-history controls, excluded inherited credentials,
  process timeout and absent-client controls. probes/README.md documents use.
- .bboxy/runs/p0-resume-probe-evidence.log — complete synthetic gate output;
  this report maps its observations to the assignment and downstream phases.

