## Limits, failures and untouched work

- No real session logs were read, copied or committed. Native fixtures, model
  input extracts and CLI output here are synthetic. Child environments exclude
  inherited authentication and seat capability; no request headers are recorded.
  Real ~/.claude and ~/.codex are not read or written by these probes. There is
  no credential setup, prompt, global install or operator step.
- Model endpoints bind only 127.0.0.1. Dummy-key requests receive canned SSE;
  external HTTP proxy settings point to a closed loopback port. Codex plugin
  synchronization, host skill discovery and dependency installation are disabled.
- Each CLI call and RPC has a 25-second deadline, import completion 10 seconds,
  and app-server shutdown 5 seconds. Timeout is a failing test, never a passing
  negative. The gate exercises process-group timeout cancellation itself.
- Tests establish CLI replay, not acceptance by a live paid model endpoint.
  Tools, images, signed thinking, encrypted reasoning/compaction, very long cwd
  slugs, interactive TUI resume, and complete same-provider byte identity are
  untested. No product parser/lowerer or source/model contract was implemented.
- This P0 branch starts from the records-only bootstrap. There is no Rust crate,
  formal model, Yarn/TLC backend or pre-existing test target on that base. Formal
  bootstrap and crate inventory remain P1's scoped deliverables; this gate
  neither claims a formal pass nor installs a fake passing formal target.
- Discovery failures corrected before the recorded gate: the initial slash-only
  Claude cwd slug gave CLI exit 1 (no conversation); replacing all nonalphanumeric
  characters fixed lookup. The first source-header check replaced URL `//` too,
  giving `make test` exit 2; converting only comment prefixes corrected the check.
- Another executor changed the shared clone to p1-bootstrap-ir during discovery.
  P0 was copied into the isolated p0 worktree before committing. Bootstrap files
  and the shared checkout were left intact. E6 was told which root files were P0
  remnants; its application acknowledgement was observed. Only P0 paths enter
  this commit. P1 will need to combine its canonical test prerequisites with
  `test-probes` when these independently based branches are integrated.
- No merge, release, publication of a package, spec amendment, or real-client
  directory change is included. The PR is the reviewable handoff to the Oracle.
